NAME
    distab - disassembler opcode table (//#use distab, ;#use distab)

SYNOPSIS
    //#use distab       C:   cc splices /lib/lib_distab.c into disasm.c
    ;#use distab        asm: appended to disasm.asm

DESCRIPTION
    The opcode table the disassembler (man disasm) reads: one record per
    opcode giving its number, its operand SHAPE, and its mnemonic. The C
    twin exposes three parallel arrays (dt_op[], dt_sh[], dt_mn[]) plus
    the count dt_n; the asm twin is a byte table DISTAB scanned by
    DIS_FIND -- `.byte <opcode>,<shape>` then `.asciiz "MNEMONIC"`, with
    $FF ending it.

    GENERATED. Both are emitted from the microcode opcode table by
    `generators/gen_p8xdis.py` (--asm for the include). Do NOT edit them
    by hand -- they are the disassembler's half of the ONE opcode source
    of truth (genucode.py's table; see hard rule 3). Add or change an
    instruction there and regenerate, so the assembler, the emulator and
    the disassembler never disagree about a mnemonic or encoding.

SEE ALSO
    disasm, asm, dump
